    "['opcode [parameter1] end', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'segment-routing prefix-sid index 1', 'parent_command': ['router isis [parameter1]', 'mpls traffic-eng router-id [parameter1]', 'segment-routing srv6'], 'root': 'router isis [parameter1]', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': '##\\nsegment-routing prefix-sid index 1\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\nThe Huawei `opcode ::1 end` command assigns a static SID (Segment Identifier) with value ::1 and marks it as an \"end\" SID (which represents the router itself in SRv6). The equivalent Cisco command uses `segment-routing prefix-sid index` to assign a prefix SID, where the index value corresponds to the SID value (1 in this case).', 'trans_template': 'segment-routing prefix-sid index 1'}]]": 1,
